# VaultSeek architecture and efficiency

Before editing, read `AGENTS.md`, `STANDING_RULES.md`, `PROJECT_CONTEXT.md`,
`CHANGELOG_DECISIONS.md`, and the directly relevant detailed documentation.

- For a task affecting three or more files or core logic, give a plan of at most
  five bullets and wait for approval or adjustments before implementation,
  unless the active task already explicitly authorizes implementation.
- Read only the directly affected modules and contracts. Work in small,
  testable chunks; avoid unrelated refactors.
- Keep replies concise: use file paths, symbols, changed functions, and test
  results. Do not paste whole files unless explicitly asked.
- UI uses Container services; Providers only communicate with external systems.
  Keep configuration typed and preserve nested acquisition values with
  `dataclasses.replace`.
- Before completing significant work, make a minimal update to project memory
  if shared facts changed; record architectural decisions in
  `CHANGELOG_DECISIONS.md` and detailed ADRs in `docs/DECISIONS.md`.
